en_ai.completion.0.content': "We are given the second-order linear differential equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{d^2x}{dt^2} + p(t)\\frac{dx}{dt} + q(t)x = 0\n\\]\n\nand told that the Wronskian \\( W(t) = x_1(t)x_2'(t) - x_1'(t)x_2(t) \\) of two solutions is a non-zero constant.\n\n**Step 1: Recall Abel's theorem**  \nFor a second-order linear ODE of the form  \n\\[\nx'' + p(t)x' + q(t)x = 0,\n\\]  \nAbel's theorem states that the Wronskian satisfies:\n\n\\[\nW(t) = W(t_0) \\exp\\left( -\\int_{t_0}^t p(s)\\, ds \\right).\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Apply the given condition**  \nWe are told \\( W(t) \\) is a non-zero constant, say \\( W(t) = C \\neq 0 \\).  \nThus:\n\n\\[\nC = W(t_0) \\exp\\left( -\\int_{t_0}^t p(s)\\, ds \\right).\n\\]\n\nSince \\( C \\) and \\( W(t_0) \\) are constants, the exponential factor must be constant for all \\( t \\). That means:\n\n\\[\n\\exp\\left( -\\int_{t_0}^t p(s)\\, ds \\right) = \\text{constant}.\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Conclude about \\( p(t) \\)**  \nThe only way the exponential of an integral is constant for all \\( t \\) is if the integral itself is constant, which implies:\n\n\\[\n\\int_{t_0}^t p(s)\\, ds = \\text{constant}.\n\\]\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to \\( t \\):\n\n\\[\np(t) = 0.\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Final answer**  \nThus, for the Wronskian to be constant, we must have:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{p(t) = 0}\n\\]\n\nfor all \\( t \\)."}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'openai.chat.completion', 'context': {'trace_id': '0xf2455e35d8f0ede609449e387576696f', 'span_id': '0x2e316c45be28559f', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.CLIENT', 'parent_id': '0x141ed3147637a66f', 'start_time': '2026-08-25T06:21:58.465961Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T06:21:59.664214Z', 'status': {'status_code': 'OK'}, 'attributes': {'gen_ai.request.type': 'chat', 'gen_ai.system': 'OpenAI',